//
// This file carries no YAML header. A header ahead of the first line becomes a
// question on import. The exception to format rule 3 and its reason stand in
// ../en.md, section 5. These lines carry what the header would have carried.
//
// Twelve scored questions, which is the number in the meta.yaml. The text
// before them is a description and is not scored.
// No standard wording, neither from the requirement nor from the guidance.

$CATEGORY: iso-iec-27003

::Note before the following questions::
The following questions check whether an implementation can be traced back to
the requirement it hangs off, and whether requirement and guidance are kept
apart. References are by standard, clause and edition.

// 1

::Binding or not::
Certification is against ISO/IEC 27003\:2017.{FALSE
####Wrong. Certification is against ISO/IEC 27001\:2022. This standard is
guidance, and a departure from it is not a nonconformity.}

// 2

::The clause for the scope::
In which clause of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 is the scope required?{
=4.3 #Right.
~4.1 #That is the external and internal issues.
~6.2 #That is the objectives.
~8.1 #That is carrying it out in operation.
####The scope belongs to the context and is the first determination of the
management system.}

// 3

::The direction when reading::
Which order is the right one when an implementation is stuck?{
=Read the requirement, write down what you understood, then take the guidance
beside it. #Right.
~Read the guidance from front to back first, then the requirement. #Read from
the front the guidance is a second table of contents.
~Read only the guidance, because it is fuller. #Then a recommendation is turned
into an obligation.
~Read only the requirement and leave the guidance out. #Then the question how
you recognise the requirement is met stays open.
####The guidance explains a place. Without your own reading of the requirement
the subject it explains is missing.}

// 4

::Tracing back with no result::
No clause can be named for an existing part of the ISMS. Which two conclusions
are permitted?{
~%50%Something stands there that nobody asked for. #Right.
~%50%A requirement is unmet somewhere else and this part shows it. #Right.
~%-100%The part is thereby wrong and gets removed. #The reason is looked for
first; an organisation may do more than is required.
~%-100%The guidance is incomplete. #The guidance is not the measure of what is
required.
####Both conclusions lead to a question. The finding is cheaper when it arises
before an audit.}

// 5

::Two editions::
Which year is the edition of ISO/IEC 27003 from that this training covers?{#2017:0
####The requirements it belongs to stand in the 2022 edition. So the guidance is
written against the previous edition of the requirements.}

// 6

::Clause and activity::
Assign to each activity the clause of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 that requires it.{
=Internal audit -> 9.2
=Management review -> 9.3
=Documented information -> 7.5
=Scope -> 4.3
####Clauses 4 to 10 carry the requirements. Anyone knowing the rough division
finds the place without searching the whole standard.}

// 7

::Departing from the guidance::
An organisation implements a clause differently from what the guidance suggests
and meets the requirement in doing so. What follows for an audit?{
=Nothing, because the check is against the requirement. #Right.
~A nonconformity, because the guidance was not followed. #Guidance is no audit
measure.
~A recommendation appearing in the report as a departure. #A departure from
guidance is no finding about the requirement.
~The certification rests until it is adjusted. #There is no ground for that.
####The measure is ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 and beside it what the organisation
determined itself.}

// 8

::What the guidance does not supply::
This standard describes a document structure an organisation has to adopt.{FALSE
####Wrong. It describes none, and the templates of this repository do not come
from it.}

// 9

::The handle for finding a place::
The requirements of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 stand in clauses {=4 to 10 ~1 to 3 ~5 to
8 ~4 to 8}.{####The clauses before them carry scope, references and terms and
are not audited.}

// 10

::What the guidance does in an argument::
Two people argue about the reach of a requirement. What does the guidance help
with?{
=It gives a text both sides can recognise. #Right.
~It settles the argument bindingly. #Only the requirement is binding.
~It replaces the decision of the leadership. #The decision stays with the
organisation.
~It shows who is right. #It supplies the questions, not the verdict.
####Almost every argument about building an ISMS is an argument about the reach
of a requirement, and a jointly recognised text is cheaper than an opinion.}

// 11

::Your own reading first::
What is the step called that stands between reading the requirement and opening
the guidance?{
=Writing down what you understood
=writing down what you understood
=Writing down your own reading
####Without that step you read the guidance as the requirement and do not notice,
because you have no sentence of your own to compare it with.}

// 12

::A scope that says too little::
The sentence "The ISMS holds for IT" is put forward. Write in two sentences how
it shows that this sentence is not enough, and what it has to carry in
addition.{
####Model answer. The sentence names a department and not a subject, and it
leaves open whether a service provider belongs in it or not. It has to name the
service, name the interfaces to third parties and say what lies expressly
outside, ISO/IEC 27001\:2022, 4.3.}
